---
const normal = Array.from({length: 12}, (_, i) => ({x: 32 + (i % 4)*45, y: 38 + Math.floor(i/4)*45}));
const abnormal = Array.from({length: 25}, (_, i) => ({x: 25+(i%5)*33+(Math.floor(i/5)%2)*8, y: 25+Math.floor(i/5)*30}));
---
<figure class="cell-growth"><div class="cell-comparison"><div><h3>Normal cell growth</h3><svg viewBox="0 0 210 165" role="img" aria-label="Evenly arranged cells illustrating controlled cell growth">{normal.map(c => <g><circle cx={c.x} cy={c.y} r="17" fill="#cfedef" stroke="#00838b" stroke-width="1.5"/><circle cx={c.x} cy={c.y} r="5" fill="#00838b"/></g>)}</svg><p>Growth follows normal controls.</p></div><div><h3>Abnormal cell growth</h3><svg viewBox="0 0 210 165" role="img" aria-label="Crowded overlapping cells illustrating uncontrolled cell growth">{abnormal.map((c,i) => <g><circle cx={c.x} cy={c.y} r={17+i%4} fill="#dfd9ef" stroke="#735ba2" stroke-width="1.5"/><circle cx={c.x} cy={c.y} r={6+i%3} fill="#735ba2"/></g>)}</svg><p>Altered cells can multiply without usual controls.</p></div></div><figcaption>Conceptual illustration, not to scale. Cell appearance varies by cancer type.</figcaption></figure>
<style>.cell-growth{margin:28px 0 0;background:#f2f9fc;border:1px solid #d9e8ef;padding:24px;border-radius:22px}.cell-comparison{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.cell-comparison>div+div{border-left:1px solid #d9e8ef;padding-left:20px}.cell-comparison h3{font-size:.95rem;letter-spacing:-.02em}.cell-comparison svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.cell-comparison p{font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.5;margin:12px 0 0}.cell-growth figcaption{font-size:.72rem;line-height:1.5;color:#53647b;margin-top:20px}@media(max-width:390px){.cell-growth{padding:17px}.cell-comparison{gap:12px}.cell-comparison>div+div{padding-left:12px}}</style>
